Error [E0119]: there's no type called `View`
  --> tests/ui/view_function_value_erases_provenance.jet:1:28
    |
  1 | fn first(values: [Int]) => View<Int> = values[0..1]
    |                            ^^^^^^^^^
 Why: generic types must name a struct or enum you defined
 Fix: check the spelling, or define the type first

Error [E0119]: `View` isn't generic
  --> tests/ui/view_function_value_erases_provenance.jet:1:28
    |
  1 | fn first(values: [Int]) => View<Int> = values[0..1]
    |                            ^^^^^^^^^
 Why: only types declared with type parameters accept `<…>`
 Fix: use `View` without type arguments

Error [E2305]: a function value cannot return a stored or borrowed view
  --> tests/ui/view_function_value_erases_provenance.jet:5:15
    |
  5 |     result :: callback(values)
    |               ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: function-value types do not carry the public owner provenance needed to prove which argument keeps the result alive
 Fix: call the named view-returning function or method directly so sema can compose its source contract
